workedExamples.question_text:
A right-angled triangle has hypotenuse $5$ and a side of length $5x$, where $0<x<1$. Angle $A$ is opposite this side, and $B$ is the other acute angle. Find expressions for $A$ and $B$, then deduce that $\arcsin x+\arccos x=\frac{\pi}{2}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm]
\draw[draw=black] (0,0)--(4,0)--(4,3)--cycle;
\draw[draw=black] (3.7,0)--(3.7,0.3)--(4,0.3);
\draw[draw=black] (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=36.87,radius=0.65];
\draw[draw=black] (4,2.4) arc[start angle=270,end angle=216.87,radius=0.6];
\path (2,1.5) node[above left,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$5$};
\path (4,1.5) node[right,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$5x$};
\path (0.9,0.28) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$A$};
\path (3.72,2.15) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
